      "run_notes": "- our ref: MI-IR-2614; issue date 24 March 2026; Issue 1, final\n- client: Ostrand Energy Networks; contact Ms Delphine Okonkwo-Hart\n- author: Maren Lisk; checker: Priya Venn; approver: Callum Draycott\n- site: Tallow Cross 132 kV substation; T2 transformer stays in service throughout\n- why: Harrowby Developments building a sheet-piled basement 14 m east of the compound fence\n- arrays: 2 x Lumenstrand LS-8, 16 gratings (14 bonded + 2 SFR); serials LS8-2614-01, -02; gratings 1.2 m apart\n- TX-A = transformer T2 plinth, east face; TX-B = cable tunnel portal, east wall\n- interrogator: Prisma FI-4 PF4-2291 in the relay room cabinet; 110 V auxiliary supply via fused spur fitted by Ostrand's electricians; 8 h UPS; 4G router outside the compound fence\n- install: 9 Mar TX-A (permit PTW-TC-0311); 10 Mar TX-B (PTW-TC-0312); 11 Mar conduit, cabinet, commissioning (PTW-TC-0313); all under Ostrand permits to work\n- fibre leads dielectric, so no bonding or earthing near live plant; armoured conduit to the cabinet\n- baseline window: 13 Mar 2026 00:00 to 16 Mar 2026 00:00; 4,320 readings per grating\n- T2 load 41-68% during the baseline; plinth surface up to +6 °C each afternoon; compensated residual within ±1.1 µε\n- baseline wavelengths: TX-A-1 1529.8371 nm sd 0.7; TX-A-2 1534.6773 nm sd 0.9; TX-A-3 1539.3976 nm sd 0.8; TX-A-4 1543.4224 nm sd 0.9; TX-A-5 1548.0537 nm sd 1.0; TX-A-6 1552.3459 nm sd 0.4; TX-A-7 1557.3574 nm sd 0.9; TX-A-8 1561.5755 nm (SFR); TX-B-1 1530.1016 nm sd 0.6; TX-B-2 1534.3521 nm sd 0.7; TX-B-3 1538.6371 nm sd 0.7; TX-B-4 1543.4900 nm sd 0.9; TX-B-5 1548.3121 nm sd 0.5; TX-B-6 1552.7570 nm sd 0.8; TX-B-7 1556.7341 nm sd 0.4; TX-B-8 1561.1832 nm (SFR)\n- designer's allowable strain change (Ostrand asset protection engineer): TX-A 180 µε; TX-B 220 µε\n- alarms to: Ms Okonkwo-Hart, Ostrand control room at Hessle, Marrick duty engineer\n- commissioning: return loss TX-A 47 dB, TX-B 45 dB; peak width 0.21 / 0.24 nm; SFRs free; conduit sealed; alarm test message received 12 Mar 2026 15:10\n- maintenance access needs an Ostrand permit to work and an authorised person on site\n",
